NAME
    copflow - log and analyze CPU/coprocessor register-window traffic

SYNOPSIS
    copflow on [<size>]
    copflow off
    copflow clear
    copflow tail [<n>]
    copflow stats
    copflow poll

DESCRIPTION
    Logs reads and writes across a cartridge coprocessor's register window
    (address, direction, value, frame number, and initiating side) to
    diagnose handshake failures and stuck status-bit polling loops.

    While armed, 'copflow' maintains per-register read/write totals across
    the entire armed interval plus a bounded ring buffer of recent
    accesses. 'copflow tail' reads from the ring buffer, while 'stats' and
    'poll' summarize the whole armed run. When disarmed, logging incurs
    minimal overhead and does nothing on cartridges without a coprocessor.

OPTIONS
    on [<size>]
        Start logging register-window traffic, optionally setting the ring
        buffer size.

    off
        Stop logging while retaining collected entries and statistics.

    clear
        Discard all recorded entries, totals, and poll-run tracking.

    tail [<n>]
        Print the most recent <n> accesses in chronological order
        (default 20).

    stats
        Print per-register read and write tallies ordered busiest first.

    poll
        Report the longest unbroken run of consecutive reads of a single
        register returning the same unchanged value, plus any active run.
        Any write from either side breaks a poll run.

EXAMPLES
    copflow on
    copflow tail 40
    copflow stats
    copflow poll
    copflow off

EXIT STATUS
    0   Command completed (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, invalid argument, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    cophist(1), cpus(1), regs(1), dma(1), watch(1)
